        <history>
          <p>Setting Walt Whitman's poem of the same name, Sea Drift is widely regarded as one of Delius's finest achievements, combining choral writing, a baritone soloist, and Delius's characteristic harmonic language to evoke a sea-bird's lament. Its German premiere preceded its English one by two years, reflecting Delius's stronger early reputation in Germany than in his native England.</p>
          <eventList type="performances">
